## Run the frontend

```
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:5173 — API calls are proxied to the backend on port 8000.
{{#if auth}}

**Admin access:** new signups are always customers — nobody becomes admin by
registering. To become the site owner:

1. Sign up on the website, then open `/dashboard`.
2. In the **Claim admin access** card, enter your owner setup code
   (Django: `ADMIN_ACCESS_CODE` in `backend/config/settings.py`;
   .NET: `AdminAccessCode` in `backend/appsettings.json`).
3. It works once, while no admin exists yet. Afterwards, open `/admin` to
   manage users{{#if shop}}, products{{/if}}{{#if contact}} and messages{{/if}},
   and promote further admins from **Admin → Users**.

Recovery without the code (needs server access): Django
`python manage.py promote_admin --email owner@example.com` (or
`createsuperuser`); .NET `dotnet run -- promote-admin --email owner@example.com`.
{{/if}}
{{#if django}}

## Run the backend (Django)

```
cd backend
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py seed_demo
python manage.py runserver
```

There is also a full admin panel at http://localhost:8000/admin/ — create a login with:

```
python manage.py createsuperuser
```

(or register through the website, then claim admin in `/dashboard` with your
owner setup code — or `python manage.py promote_admin --email you@example.com`).
{{/if}}
{{#if dotnet}}

## Run the backend (ASP.NET Core)

Requires the .NET 10 SDK.

```
cd backend
dotnet run
```

The database is created and seeded automatically at http://localhost:8000.
Interactive API docs: http://localhost:8000/swagger
{{/if}}
